# Commit Message Guidelines - docs (Mintlify KB + synced Terraform provider docs)
# Auto-ignored lines begin with "#"
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Summary (Required):
# - Concise, imperative summary (e.g., Sync AWS provider docs to v6.57.1)
# - No issue numbers or PR refs here
#
# Type(scope): common types - feat, fix, docs, chore, refactor, test
# Scopes (docs repo): infra, runbooks, references, providers, mintlify
#   - use 'providers' for terraform-providers/ syncs (e.g., chore(providers): ...)

# Body (Optional):
# - Context, motivation, implementation details; bullets OK

# Tags (Optional) - add at bottom if relevant:
#   BREAKING CHANGE / SECURITY / BUGFIX / DOCS / REFACTOR / INFRA / COMPLIANCE

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# If found, reset the commit with:
#   git reset HEAD~ && git commit --edit

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RECON DISCIPLINE - apply at composition time (checklist; not auto-enforced)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# NEVER include in the commit message:
#   - Cloud account IDs (use first-2/last-2 redaction if context is required)
#   - Cloud project IDs (specific GCP/AWS/Azure resource identifiers)
#   - Service account emails
#   - 1Password vault names, item names, or op:// paths
#   - Specific IAM principal names (users, roles, policies)
#   - Specific secret names (Secret Manager IDs, KMS key aliases)
#   - Internal hostnames (server names not visible to customers)
#   - Local file paths (absolute paths to operator workstations)
#   - AI reviewer / assistant names (Codex, Gemini, Claude, etc.)
#   - Co-authored-by: <AI> trailers
#   - Session-tag enumeration or other architecture-mapping recon
#
# DO include:
#   - WHAT changed (feature, scope, behavior)
#   - WHY it changed (constraint, upstream release, breaking-change driver)
#   - Pattern references when relevant
#   - Operational properties when relevant
#
# Team attribution: Team TECPRESSO. Never AI-specific attribution.
# Full conventions: ~/workspace/CLAUDE.md + ~/workspace/CLAUDE/conventions.md
